# Multilingual Synchronization Rules

- French at the root (`index.html`, `pages/*.html`) is the primary source of truth for the website.
- Whenever any change (content, layout, structure, or design) is made, always apply it across all 3 languages: French (`index.html`, `pages/*.html`), English (`en/index.html`, `en/pages/*.html`), and Arabic (`ar/index.html`, `ar/pages/*.html`).
- Maintain full parity across all 3 versions, respecting `dir="rtl"` and proper translation context.

